      "type": "Feature",
      "properties": {
        "project_name": "Stack Plaza",
        "site": "Potrero Power Station",
        "status": "planned",
        "use": "park",
        "geometry_type": "approximate",
        "digitized_from": "Built by Pier & Point from the edges around it rather than traced from the Design for Development's own drawing: the part of Assessor lot 4175028 south of Block 9's south edge (extended to the shore), less the shoreline strip kept as Waterfront Park, The Point and the two roadside lots 4232015 and 4232016. The Design for Development labels it (3) 'Stack Plaza' on Figure 4.16.1 (printed p.93) and gives it Section 4.21 and Figure 4.21.2.",
        "digitization_method": "CREATED 2026-10-11 (at the owner's direction). Lot 4175028 (DataSF, 21,885 m2) was cut at the straight line along Block 9's south edge (the edge of our Block 9 drawing between (554436.1, 4178929.7) and (554475.2, 4178933.1), EPSG:26910, extended east to the shore); from the part south of that line, the Waterfront Park strip, The Point and lots 4232015 and 4232016 were removed. Result 1,810 m2 (0.45 acre), all inside lot 4175028. It contains 242 m2 of the existing Stack drawing. The Design for Development's circular amphitheater around the smokestack was not georeferenced, so the plaza's real outline may differ.",
        "accuracy_caveat": "APPROXIMATE, DIRECTIONAL -- this outline comes from the lot and from neighbouring shapes, not from the Design for Development's drawing of Stack Plaza, so its edges may differ from the planned plaza by tens of metres. The SF Planning project page lists 'The ~0.6-acre \"Stack Plaza\"'; this shape is about 0.45 acre. It overlaps the existing Stack drawing on purpose (the plaza is planned around the smokestack).",
        "why_no_real_parcel": "No Assessor lot of its own: the shape lies wholly inside DataSF's active lot 4175028 (21,885 m2, 1241 Delaware St, PPS-MU zoning), an undivided lot that also holds Blocks 3, 4 and 9, Humboldt Street Plaza and parts of the shoreline parks (checked 2026-10-11).",
        "regulatory_context": "Open space (3) in the Design for Development's Waterfront Open Spaces: Section 4.21 'Stack Plaza' (Figure 4.21.2, enlargement concept plan).",
        "notes": "Added 2026-10-11 as its own record; it was previously only named inside Waterfront Park's record. Status 'planned': no source read gives a construction date.",
        "images": [],
        "source_doc_urls": [
          "https://sfplanning.org/sites/default/files/documents/citywide/potreropower_D4D_final.pdf",
          "https://sfplanning.org/project/potrero-power-station"
        ]
      },
